INPUT    : MAINFRAME
REVERSED : EMARFNIAM


IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. REVERSE.

DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 WS-INPUT PIC X(20) VALUE 'MAINFRAME'
01 WS-REVERSED PIC X(20).

PROCEDURE DIVISION.
  MOVE FUNCTION REVERSE(WS-INPUT) TO WS-REVERSED

DISPLAY 'INPUT : 'WS-INPUT
DISPLAY 'REVERSED : 'WS-REVERSED

STOP RUN.

*********************************************************** 
01 WS-INPUT PIC X(20) VALUE 'MAINFRAME'.
       01 WS-OUTPUT PIC X(20).
       01 I PIC 99.
       01 J PIC 99.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.

           MOVE 1 TO J

           PERFORM VARYING I FROM 9 BY -1
               UNTIL I < 1

               MOVE WS-INPUT(I:1)
                 TO WS-OUTPUT(J:1)

               ADD 1 TO J

           END-PERFORM

           DISPLAY 'INPUT    : ' WS-INPUT
           DISPLAY 'REVERSED : ' WS-OUTPUT

           STOP RUN.

INPUT    : MAINFRAME
REVERSED : EMARFNIAM

Explanation for interview
1. I starts from the last character (9).
2. Read characters from right to left.
3. J starts from position 1.
4. Move each character into the output field.
5. Repeat until all characters are reversed.

Important interview concept:
WS-INPUT(I:1) means read one character from position I.
WS-OUTPUT(J:1) means move one character to position J.

